# Creating Cursor Rules: never .md, always .mdc in .cursor/rules

When creating new MDC rules for this project, always:

1. Save the rule as a separate Markdown file in the `.cursor/rules` directory
2. Give the file a descriptive name related to the rule's purpose
3. Follow the MDC rule format with appropriate frontmatter (title, description)
4. Include clear instructions in the body of the rule

## Rule Management Workflow

- **Edit existing rules** when updating content that matches an existing topic or rule
- **Create new rule files** only for completely new topics or guidelines that don't fit within existing rules
- **Never duplicate rule content** across multiple files

## Example structure:

```markdown
---
title: Rule Title
description: Brief description of what the rule does
---

# Rule Title

[Detailed instructions for the rule]
```

Remember that each rule should be in its own separate file to maintain clarity and allow for easier updates.